## Commands

### Official scaffold command

From repo root:

```bash
hatch factory init \
  --id {{factory_id}} \
  --repo {{target_repo}} \
  --control-plane {{control_plane_repo}} \
  --runs-dir {{runs_dir}}
```

Use `--force` only when intentionally re-scaffolding:

```bash
hatch factory init \
  --id {{factory_id}} \
  --repo {{target_repo}} \
  --control-plane {{control_plane_repo}} \
  --runs-dir {{runs_dir}} \
  --force
```

### Immediate validation commands

```bash
pnpm test -- apps/hatch/src/factory/scaffold.test.ts apps/hatch/src/factory/init.test.ts
# Full conformance gate (config schema, graph validation, recovery ownership, run-dir isolation)
pnpm test -- apps/hatch/src/factory/conformance-harness.test.ts
pnpm docs:check
pnpm docs:state:check
```

## Policy-pack contract

The `policy-pack/v1/` directory is scaffolded with required shared keys. Do not remove `shared.*` keys — they are platform-owned defaults.

Read the authoritative contract before customizing:
- `docs/skills/factory-authoring/policy-pack.md`

Allowed local overrides live under `factory.*` keys in each policy JSON file and in `factory.config.json → policyPack.overrides`.

